1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
ジューキャロン

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Oh

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
See you next time.

4
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,020
Captain, may I ask you a question?

5
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,040
And Queen to F3.

6
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:37,600
Alright. King to G7.

7
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,880
Is it a good idea to send me into battle?

8
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,380
Rook to E4.

9
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:46,640
If I should get killed, the Deucalion's Alt-Noah will shut down.

10
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:49,520
Yes, I'm aware of that. Rook to D8.

11
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:52,740
But we can't worry about that until we have to.

12
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:56,840
And Zenkaiska, are you trying to ask if you can be relieved of combat duty?

13
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,960
No. I'm really well suited for it.

14
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:02,300
Now Queen to F6 and check.

15
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:05,040
King to F6. King takes your Queen.

16
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:07,200
And I would agree with your assessment.

17
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:09,820
Bishop to E5. Check.

18
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,700
I'll put it on the monitor.

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,260
Did you come up with that move all by yourself?

20
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:19,420
Or is it from that analytical engine of yours?

21
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:21,820
70% at least is me.

22
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:22,880
70%?

23
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:28,180
I'm trying to optimize its processing efficiency by assigning tasks to idle brain cells.

24
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:33,180
So it's the device's suggestion as well as my own organic idea at the same time.

25
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:36,680
Both this ship and everyone in her crew owe their lives to you.

26
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:40,760
If you believe you should be fighting, I think we should accept your judgment on that.

27
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,460
Thanks for that.

28
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:47,360
But I don't deserve any kind of special treatment.

29
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:54,100
Has anyone told you that all Noah activation tests were conducted using samples of the blood splatter from your clothing?

30
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:54,900
Hmm?

31
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,120
King to G5.

32
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,900
All unsuccessful.

33
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,700
None met the requirements for powering up.

34
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:04,540
You are a special case indeed, Ensign.

35
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:13,400
The activation factor you received when you administered emergency treatment was somehow triggered when it came into contact with Royal Blood.

36
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:21,560
Ever since the last battle, we've obtained plenty of intel on both the Martian cataphracts as well as their use of Aldnoa.

37
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:26,160
For military power, no question they have the advantage over us.

38
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:29,200
If we take them on, we'll surely be the underdogs.

39
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:33,840
If we do, Ensign Kaizka, then my money is on you.

40
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,040
Bishop to G7.

41
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,480
Do you resign, Captain?

42
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:46,180
Was that a move from you or your left eye?

43
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:48,480
I'll let you decide that for yourself.

44
00:03:57,420 --> 00:04:01,040
Well, I suppose not even the Tharsis can see that far into the future.

45
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:17,900
Carry on.

46
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:18,640
Yes, sir.

47
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:31,160
And were you successful, my lord Slane?

48
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:34,460
I clustered my shots in the region you calculated, Mr. Parklight.

49
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:35,740
Good, my lord.

50
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,740
Let's hope they're not deflected by some uncharted flux.

51
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:41,700
Ah, I thought I smelled something.

52
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,700
Looks like a dog snuck on board.

53
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,460
And a common grubby little puppy dog at that.

54
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,460
Just what are you doing here?

55
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,820
Good day, Count Muril Sion.

56
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,580
And you too, Count Barocruz.

57
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:57,500
I came because my wish is to join the battle.

58
00:04:57,780 --> 00:04:58,800
Disgusting creature.

59
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,600
You need to mind your tongue.

60
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:07,880
Count Sosboom?

61
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:10,920
Sir Slane Troyard here is my vassal.

62
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,740
If he is offended, I apologize.

63
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:20,480
However, if this action of yours is unwarranted, Count Muril Sion, it would be unfortunate.

64
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:24,280
If he were merely some pet, it would be barely tolerable.

65
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:28,620
But to actually make him a knight, that's taking your game a little too far.

66
00:05:28,940 --> 00:05:34,220
Count Barocruz, you do not have the privilege of offering opinions regarding my vassals.

67
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,980
Fighting alongside him is another matter entirely.

68
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:41,540
One cannot take to the field of battle with a traitor at your back.

69
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:45,460
Well then, go ahead and strike me down right now.

70
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:47,860
You are entirely correct.

71
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:53,280
If I went into battle with you, it's almost certain I would be struck from behind.

72
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,520
How dare you!

73
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:57,900
Everyone, hear my words!

74
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:07,940
By the grace of the Emperor of Verse, here and now I name the knight slain Troyard as my son.

75
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:12,020
Every one of you here bears witness to this!

76
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,660
My lord count-

77
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:15,640
Stand, Slane.

78
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:19,420
From this day forward, you are my son.

79
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:24,700
And do you still wish to raise a hand to him now, Count Muril Sion?

80
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:30,620
If you are prepared to go to such lengths, then so be it.

81
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:35,660
But if his behavior is suspicious in the slightest, there will be no mercy.

82
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:40,860
Forgive me, my lord.

83
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:43,440
I have put you in an awkward position.

84
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:44,040
No.

85
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:46,520
I had decided on this long ago.

86
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:49,360
I too could fall in battle.

87
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:51,820
I must have a successor in place.

88
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:55,040
So from now on, think of me as your father.

89
00:06:55,040 --> 00:07:07,580
Congratulations, my lord Slane.

90
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,240
Heir to Count Salzbaum.

91
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:13,960
This change puts you one step closer to your dream, my lord.

92
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,300
That is enough, Mr. Harklight.

93
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:19,680
Someone in my position has no dreams.

94
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:23,420
The time has almost come.

95
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,440
Yes, my lady.

96
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:29,380
Which side do you think will emerge victorious, Adele Ritzo?

97
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:33,960
Why, the glorious First Imperial Forces will absolutely win the day.

98
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:35,000
Of course.

99
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,020
Is that really what you want?

100
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:41,220
Don't you have friends down on Earth aboard a United Forces ship?

101
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:42,460
Friends down on Earth?

102
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:43,860
Oh, perish the thought.

103
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:46,180
Well then, how about a wager?

104
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:47,280
A wager?

105
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:50,260
If the Verse Empire wins, I bet...

106
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:51,200
Let me think.

107
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,100
I know.

108
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:54,240
I bet my sister's life.

109
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,060
I'm joking.

110
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,160
I wonder...

111
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:05,040
What are you dreaming of now, dear sister?

112
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,200
Hey, have you seen Inko?

113
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,320
Try the Electromat Catapult.

114
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:18,360
She and Raya are probably hanging out there.

115
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,080
That's great.

116
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:19,860
Thanks a bunch!

117
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:21,080
And try not to get lost.

118
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:21,680
Bye!

119
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:25,040
Damn!

120
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:26,200
Wearing sweats!

121
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,400
Yutaro, you know you're a pervert, right?

122
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:31,340
Tharsis.

123
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,560
Full ability is still unknown.

124
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,940
High percentage of attack evasion reported.

125
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,740
Current pilot has been confirmed.

126
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:44,060
Slane, Troiard.

127
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:49,020
A good luck charm given to me by a dear Terran friend when I left for Earth.

128
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,660
Animals that fly through the air!

129
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,500
Yes, Slane, it's just like you told me.

130
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,160
Does he also have a Neuralink?

131
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:59,340
An analytical engine of his own?

132
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:02,520
Must be.

133
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:04,380
But I don't have enough data.

134
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:07,440
It was dodging like it could see the future.

135
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:13,380
If that's the way things are, could be a problem.

136
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:14,540
You monologuing?

137
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:18,140
Just talking to myself.

138
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,700
That's what monologuing is!

139
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:31,880
The warrior god Odin, the rider of the eight-legged horse Sleipnir, drank the waters of Mimus Bruner and was granted vast wisdom.

140
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:36,560
But the price he paid for gaining that wisdom was his left eye.

141
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:38,660
Norse mythology.

142
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:39,940
You're quite the nerd.

143
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:42,820
Oh man, now you're just messing with me, right?

144
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:49,620
After that Russian battle we had, I just wanted to get off the ship.

145
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:52,460
I was scared to death.

146
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:57,240
But I knew if I did that, I could never look Okujo in the eye when I died.

147
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:02,300
If your horse is ever acting up, you find me day or night.

148
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:04,240
And I'll fix it up in a flash.

149
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,740
I'll hold you to that.

150
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:06,840
Alright, look.

151
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,800
Why don't we grab a bite before the battle?

152
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,680
We should have enough time for it.

153
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:12,000
I'll pass, thanks.

154
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,300
Back when I got shot, apparently my stomach was empty.

155
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:20,080
I'd have died if my other organs had been contaminated by what was in my stomach.

156
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:20,700
Really?

157
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:21,300
Ugh.

158
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:25,740
But considering, some tea would be good.

159
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:29,340
Has he chosen his wire reels yet?

160
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:30,640
Number one through number three.

161
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:32,820
Number ten in case of emergency.

162
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:35,040
One of each mounted left and right.

163
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:37,100
His specs are showing some high-G pivots.

164
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:39,300
Long, thin wires aren't optimal for that.

165
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:40,160
I found you!

166
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:42,240
If it isn't Team Decalian...

167
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:44,300
The old Noah unit everyone's on about.

168
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:46,500
They say that you're all Martians.

169
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:50,020
You don't want to get in our way on the battlefield, little ladies.

170
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:53,600
Stupid jerks.

171
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:54,860
What's their problem anyway?

172
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:56,300
But they aren't wrong.

173
00:10:57,380 --> 00:10:59,160
All Martians are the enemy.

174
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:02,720
I know that better than anyone.

175
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:08,920
You are so adorable, Rae.

176
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:11,000
Hard shell outside.

177
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:11,560
I'm what?

178
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:13,500
With a soft, gooey center.

179
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:15,160
What are you talking about?

180
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:16,160
Want to get some candy?

181
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:17,540
I'm gonna deck you.

182
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:20,540
Entering defense airspace in 30 minutes.

183
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:22,060
Clear to initiate launch.

184
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:22,680
Launch.

185
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:23,540
And good hunting.

186
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,260
Is my steed prepared?

187
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,180
All fine-tuning completed, my lord.

188
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:31,700
Good.

189
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,160
Teoscuria 2, launching!

190
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:44,440
Sir Slain Troyard, now launching the Tharsis.

191
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:48,200
Stygia Squadron, launching!

192
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,520
Martian cataphracts on approach.

193
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:03,980
Attention all forces!

194
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:05,380
We are go for action!

195
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:07,160
Message from headquarters.

196
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,560
We are a go for action.

197
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:10,800
Deucalion, launch now.

198
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:14,320
We will be providing guerrilla-style support for the attack platoons.

199
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,940
Prepare the ship for battle.

200
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:17,660
All our shipboard cataphracts.

201
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:19,520
They're being launched from Trident Base.

202
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,700
Mustang-1-1, you are clear for launch.

203
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:25,540
Roger that.

204
00:12:25,900 --> 00:12:28,380
Mustang-1-1, cleared for launch confirmed.

205
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,620
Railgun launch!

206
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:37,780
Railgun launch!

207
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:53,980
Target lock is in effect.

208
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:55,300
Now commencing the attack.

209
00:12:55,300 --> 00:13:04,320
Enemy inbound!

210
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:05,200
Hold fire!

211
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:07,720
They won't be able to hit us in this gravity flux anyway.

212
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:09,240
Fire when they get in closer!

213
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,220
Fire when they get in closer.

214
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:13,260
Fire when they get in closer!

215
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:16,440
My umbrella's been hit!

216
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:18,740
Mustang-1-1!

217
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:19,560
I'm okay.

218
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,100
Debris is bad.

219
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:23,240
I can't get a shot with this vibration!

220
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:26,480
Mustang-0-0 will assist.

221
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:33,060
Inaho!

222
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:38,340
What about your umbrella?

223
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:39,520
It's only drizzling.

224
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:40,500
I don't need it.

225
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:42,440
Stop it with your crazy stunts!

226
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:44,780
I wouldn't be able to use it in a dogfight anyway.

227
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:46,480
Infer gravity shifts.

228
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:48,120
Apply vector compensation.

229
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:49,880
Fire.

230
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:51,860
Commence attack!

231
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:56,180
Why, you?

232
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,520
Pivot via wire swing-by.

233
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,060
Returning to combat space.

234
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:08,880
Reel number three.

235
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:11,700
Fire.

236
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:18,500
Pivot in progress.

237
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:22,440
Complete in four, three, two, and one.

238
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:23,500
Release.

239
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,860
Inaho Kaisuka.

240
00:14:38,260 --> 00:14:39,780
And you slain Troyard.

241
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:47,000
Next conjunction with Marineros' base in 30 seconds.

242
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:48,800
Main guns ready to go.

243
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:50,240
Attention all platoons.

244
00:14:50,540 --> 00:14:51,920
Clear away from our line of fire.

245
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:53,180
Rye!

246
00:14:53,180 --> 00:14:56,080
This is Rhinelander 2-2.

247
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,480
I've got one of these things right on my six.

248
00:14:58,980 --> 00:14:59,980
Roger that.

249
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:01,980
Mustang 2-2 moving to assist.

250
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:09,080
It's the Martian.

251
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:11,620
Marineros' base now within range.

252
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:12,920
Field of fire is clear.

253
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:13,780
No friendlies.

254
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:15,560
Fire main guns.

255
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:24,240
Marineros' base beginning to move away.

256
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:27,700
Disengage attack platoons and guerrilla unit immediately.

257
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:29,080
Put them on defense.

258
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:31,040
Inaho, we've been ordered to disengage.

259
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:31,840
Come back.

260
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:33,680
Inaho!

261
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,880
That is some accurate shooting.

262
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:46,980
I knew it.

263
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:48,780
He's using predictions.

264
00:15:49,380 --> 00:15:50,380
Number one, pivot.

265
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:01,680
I'll wait until the moment he comes out from behind the rocks.

266
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:04,980
He will attack me the instant that I leave the protection of the rocks.

267
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:07,180
Data confirmed.

